Z||000000||Bigfieroman||01-05-2001||10:18 AM||||The beretta btz/gtu 89-92 wheels.  16X7, 42mm, on 84-87, need spacers without brake conversion, by 7 mm, or on 88 and brake conversion, no spacer necessary!  I got a set, perfect condition, from a professional slavage yard for $200<P>------------------<BR>I once got a warning from a Police officer because he couldn't keep up with me around some twisties.  the prerequisite for a warning instead of a ticket was that I must let him drive it back and forth the way we had come.  Burned a quater tank of my gas!||||reg||10
Z||000001||batboy||01-05-2001||11:44 AM||||I'm just curious, which brake conversion are you talking about? The Grand Am/Beretta swap? Why does it need a spacer on non-88 Fieros without the brake conversion?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bigfieroman||01-05-2001||12:12 PM||||The 84-87 swap moves out the wheels by 9mm, with the wheels installed it is 2mm further out. With a spacer they would be out of the wheel wells.  The 88' uses a 6 in rim in front, 35mm offset.  Adding an extra inch overall puts out the wheels 6.25mm more each way. With 7mm more offset, the outer wheel location is nearly the same.  The rears are supossedly 42mm offset already, so they are fine.  I am not sure if the rear 88' wheels are the same as the 87', so you may need the spacers on the rear only.  Confused yet?<P>------------------<BR>I once got a warning from a Police officer because he couldn't keep up with me around some twisties.  the prerequisite for a warning instead of a ticket was that I must let him drive it back and forth the way we had come.  Burned a quater tank of my gas!||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||01-05-2001||03:19 PM||||I wasn't bothering to logically think this all out. Of course you're right about moving the front wheels out a little with the swapped brakes. I have the Grand Am brakes on my Batmobile and have been looking for a set of inexpensive 15" or 16" wheels. This just might be what I'm looking for. I need to find a kid who's ricing out a Beretta GT/Grand Am GT and has an extra set of factory alloy wheels.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bigfieroman||01-05-2001||03:34 PM||||Those wheels wont work.  I am not sure, but I dont think the 15"s from the Beretta or grand am are the correct offset.  Also, the Grand am  rims are 16 X 6, thats why the tires always look so puffed out.<P>------------------<BR>I once got a warning from a Police officer because he couldn't keep up with me around some twisties.  the prerequisite for a warning instead of a ticket was that I must let him drive it back and forth the way we had come.  Burned a quater tank of my gas!||||reg||1
